			<item>
				<title>Thoughts on Linux, Neovim, Hyprland, etc.</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/blog/linux-neovim/</link>
				<pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/blog/linux-neovim/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I started tinkering with Linux (and the rest of my computer) during the COVID lockdown (like may others, I gather). My first thought was, &amp;ldquo;I want to be cool&amp;rdquo; (I was like 13 at the time) so I tried Arch first. Of course Arch Linux installation isn&amp;rsquo;t the easiest thing (especially for a dumb 7th grader) so of course I bricked my system (probably). Fortunately I had a full backup of my disk and I learned to start with something more manageable first.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
